{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791433648,"nonce":"fGzQWGDrsDvKQQ6ETsti7SRBoqA=","title":"HIR: turn small pure branch diamonds into scalar selects for Cranelift","message":"The LLVM-off NUC branchy loop retains short branch/phi diamonds for modulo sign corrections and arithmetic arms. Cranelift emits separate branches and jumps for them. The shared HIR pipeline currently merges straight-line blocks and threads empty blocks but has no small-diamond if-conversion pass.\n\nConvert bounded diamonds and triangles with scalar phis and cheap, non-trapping pure arms into Select instructions. Leave calls, loads, stores, integer division/remainder, trapping casts, shared arms and loop backedges intact. Preserve evaluation order within each arm and do not grow wide dispatch chains. Validate actual Cranelift/LLVM/interpreter answers, rejection cases, and NUC LLVM-off kernel plus whole-process timings before landing.","files":null}]}